a tense situation. It all began with the appalling news about a clothing line that was promoting the first evening. I know it's alarming, but the clothing store Holly's invests in child labor. A company that designs the wardrobes of wealthy middle-aged women relies on working children. Children who were supposed to be attending school or playing hide-and-seek. What? Doesn't the U.S. have laws about that? No folks, these children are in South East Asia. Isn't it convenient when regulations are different overseas? Aren't authorities in these countries aware of this practice? If you ask me, companies like this are supposed to use even more compassionate practices when dealing cross-culturally.", "id": 1, "image": "engenn8le04ob03re2img02.jpg"}, {"time": "65000", "text": "Like me, you may feel overwhelmed by such scenarios. But we aren't helpless, are we? No! We can start a petition at the website, TakeAStand.org. Shouldn't the organizers of the event do something about it? We can call and ask them to make a statement of apology for hosting Holly's. That's what they were supposed to do in the first place. Don't you think we should start boycotting stores that sell Holly's apparel? Post your reactions and get a dialogue going!", "id": 2, "image": "engenn8le04ob03re2img03.jpg"}], "coverimg": "engenn8le04ob03re2img01.jpg"}}], "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "id": 1}], "id": 0}]}